{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Legislate to revoke Parental Responsibility after long absence",
        "additional_details": "Resident parents who raise children without support should not be held back by the legal rights of an absent parent. Right now, a parent with no contact or involvement for years can still block simple, necessary life choices for a child, forcing the primary parent into unnecessary court battles. We believe the law must evolve to protect resident families: if a parent abandons their duties for a specified prolonged period, their legal control over that child should automatically end.",
        "background": "We want the Government to automatically review or revoke Parental Responsibility when a parent has been absent for a specified long-term period. Resident parents should not have to face costly, stressful court battles to make basic decisions for a child left by an absent parent.",
